## ggthemes library  

Next, we’ll show a few examples of how to use the predefined themes to modify the aesthetics of plots.  


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
library(ggthemes)
```
:::


<br>

### theme_wsj   

The Wall Street Journal's theme.  


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
plot + theme_wsj()
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](3_ggplot_themes_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-13-1.png){width=672}
:::
:::


<br>

### theme_tufte  

A minimalist theme inspired by the work of statistician Edward Tufte.   


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
plot + theme_tufte()
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](3_ggplot_themes_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-14-1.png){width=672}
:::
:::


<br>

### theme_solarized  

A theme that uses colors based on the solarized palette.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
plot + theme_solarized()
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](3_ggplot_themes_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-15-1.png){width=672}
:::
:::


<br>


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
plot + theme_solarized(light = FALSE)
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](3_ggplot_themes_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-16-1.png){width=672}
:::
:::


<br>

### theme_gdocs  

A theme with Google Docs Chart defaults.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
plot + theme_gdocs()
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](3_ggplot_themes_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-17-1.png){width=672}
:::
:::


<br>

### theme_fivethirtyeight  

Theme inspired by fivethirtyeight.com plots.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
